## What was done

All six quick wins from `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-13-playground-build-inspection-audit.md`
line 72, implemented mini-app-only (no `apps/api`, no `packages/shared`, no migrations).

1. **starterPrompts per bot + Rori empty state.** `ChatPanel`'s render path already
   existed; what was missing was data and callers. `features/rori/starter-prompts.ts`
   now holds a per-bot lookup (`getStarterPromptsForBot`) covering Rori,
   `document_wizard`, `tutor`, `verifier`, `tax_legal_research`; wired at **both**
   `ChatPanel` call sites (`RoriWorkspace.tsx`, `DashboardShell.tsx`). `hideEmptyState`
   removed from Rori's call site only. `form_wizard` intentionally unmapped (routes to
   `FormWizardPanel`, never reaches `ChatPanel`); unknown ids fall back to `[]`.
2. **Thinking bubble.** Rendered in `ChatPanel` while `submitting`, positioned after
   `visibleMessages` so it is visible under `latestExchangeOnly` (Rori's mode); empty
   state gated with `!submitting` so the two cannot overlap; respects `prefersReducedMotion`.
3. **Telegram BackButton / haptics / closing confirmation / themeParams.** New helpers
   in `lib/telegram.ts` (`setTelegramBackButton`, `triggerTelegramHaptic`,
   `setTelegramClosingConfirmation`, `computeThemeCssVariables`, `applyTelegramThemeParams`),
   all fully optional-chained; wired in `DashboardShell` (BackButton bound to the
   existing `handleBackToMenu`, closing confirmation scoped to `isSessionActive`,
   themeParams applied once on mount) and `ChatPanel` (haptic on send).
4. **Low-time nudges.** Pure `getLowTimeNudgeThreshold(remainingSeconds, isSessionActive)`
   using `<=600`/`<=120` threshold-crossing (not equality) plus a per-session
   fired-once `Set` latch reset on `activeSessionId` change. 1s polling interval
   untouched (TASK-012).
5. **Codex OAuth auto-poll.** 4000ms interval in `ProviderConnectPanel`, sharing a
   pure `resolveCodexOAuthPollAction` with the existing manual button. Stops on
   connected / expired / failed / unmount / provider-switch.
6. **Bot descriptions before selection.** Static always-visible `<ul class="menu-specialist-guide">`
   under the hex artboard plus description in each hex button's `aria-label` — not
   hover-gated.

