## QC review outcome

Blank-context reviewer returned 3 findings; adjudications fully written up in
`reports/TASK-011-qc-review-cycle1.md`.

- **Findings 1 and 3 — DISMISSED.** Both flagged the `fetchLaunchContext` header
  cutover in `lib/telegram.ts`. That hunk is **TASK-010's**, already auditor-signed-off
  at revision 8 and still uncommitted in the tree. **This was my error**: I froze the
  reviewer's diff with `git diff -- apps/telegram-miniapp`, which necessarily included
  TASK-010's mini-app changes, and my prompt excluded only `apps/api`. The reviewer read
  the diff correctly; I scoped it wrongly, costing two of its three findings.
  Independently of attribution, the failure scenario cannot occur: the backend reads
  the header at `apps/api/src/modules/telegram/telegram.route.ts:12` and
  `apps/api/src/app.ts:255` (verified by inspecting code outside the diff).
- **Finding 2 — UPHELD and fixed.** Item 1 was Rori-only despite the audit's "per bot".
  I had independently found this before the review landed (two `ChatPanel` call sites;
  `DashboardShell.tsx:2381` passed nothing, covering Cursive/Insight/Top Secret/Condor).
  Engineer redispatched → cycle 2 closed it. One correction to the reviewer's framing:
  no per-bot prompt *data* existed anywhere; what was "already built" was the render
  path, so the fix required authoring data, not wiring an existing source.

